<item><title>Namibia wrestlers seek N$334 600 for Commonwealth championships</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/na/namibia-wrestlers-seek-n-334-600-for-commonwealth-273cbf/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/na/namibia-wrestlers-seek-n-334-600-for-commonwealth-273cbf/</guid><category>Namibia</category><description>The federation needs the funds by 27 November for accommodation, meals and a training camp in Polokwane, South Africa.</description><pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 09:55:30 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/na.jpg" length="33196" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/na.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Study projects N$313.74 billion annual GDP contribution from Namibia oil</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/na/study-projects-n-313-74-billion-annual-gdp-contribution-6ffa18/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/na/study-projects-n-313-74-billion-annual-gdp-contribution-6ffa18/</guid><category>Namibia</category><description>A Standard Bank Namibia-commissioned study ties the estimate to three offshore projects, while production has yet to begin and local benefits are not assured.</description><pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 07:15:31 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/na.jpg" length="33196" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/na.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Meatco proposes three-month wage cuts as exports remain suspended</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/na/meatco-proposes-three-month-wage-cuts-as-exports-remain-48f456/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/na/meatco-proposes-three-month-wage-cuts-as-exports-remain-48f456/</guid><category>Namibia</category><description>The state-owned processor says a 50% reduction in working hours from January would save about N$16.7 million, while December pay also faces cuts.</description><pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 06:58:36 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/na/meatco-proposes-three-month-wage-cuts-as-exports-remain-48f456/share.jpg" length="44220" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/na/meatco-proposes-three-month-wage-cuts-as-exports-remain-48f456/share.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Namibia reports N$50.3m in payment fraud through October</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/na/namibia-reports-n-50-3m-in-payment-fraud-through-october-0fb7ed/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/na/namibia-reports-n-50-3m-in-payment-fraud-through-october-0fb7ed/</guid><category>Namibia</category><description>The Bank of Namibia says card, electronic funds transfer and electronic-money channels recorded the losses, with EFT fraud driving a first-half increase.</description><pubDate>Tue, 24 Nov 2026 14:59:16 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/na.jpg" length="33196" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/na.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
